`lastModifiedId` for nested blocks uses index-based IDs (e.g., `${sectionId}-nested-${nestedIndex}`) but never resets. After a delete or reorder shifts indices, the persistent warning-border highlight lands on the wrong block indefinitely.

## Changes

- **`BlockList.tsx`** — Added `triggerLastModified(id)` helper backed by `lastModifiedTimeoutRef` that auto-clears `lastModifiedId` after 3 s, mirroring the existing `justDroppedId` / `dropHighlightTimeoutRef` pattern. Cancels any in-flight timeout on re-trigger. Timeout cleaned up in the existing unmount `useEffect`.

```ts
const triggerLastModified = useCallback((id: string) => {
  if (lastModifiedTimeoutRef.current) {
    clearTimeout(lastModifiedTimeoutRef.current);
  }
  setLastModifiedId(id);
  lastModifiedTimeoutRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
    setLastModifiedId(null);
    lastModifiedTimeoutRef.current = null;
  }, 3000);
}, []);
```

All four `setLastModifiedId(id)` call sites (root edit, root duplicate, nested section edit, conditional branch edit) replaced with `triggerLastModified(id)`.

> Note: The reported `blockIndex` dead-code issue does not exist in the merged codebase — only `blockNumber` is defined and referenced in `getBlockItemStyles`. No action required.

